
Changes made to ipwman -- August 1992 by Dana Jacobsen, ERL-C

-----

Changed to allow ipwman to get information on all additional files
by reading $IPW/exp/*/bin and $IPW/exp/*/lib in addition to the
standard directories.

Use the PAGER variable if it exists instead of assuming more.

Don't automatically strip out all the spaces in front of manual
sections.  Some people use spaces instead of tabs and this 
reformatted their man sections into garbage, while providing
no benefit.  I changed this to remove 0 or 1 space instead of all.

-----

Changes made April 1993 by Dana Jacobsen, ERL-C

Put a sed '$d' right before calling the pager.  This removes the last ^L
which would cause a blank page to get printed.  The purpose of the control
L is to seperate man pages if more than one is asked for.  This is nice, but
we really shouldn't have one at the end.
